# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# Two reasons, and the second is the one that matters. Speed: bin/ and obj/ across forty projects
# is most of the bytes the daemon would otherwise copy. Secrecy: a build context is readable by
# every layer of the build, and `.env`, `.git` and a stray `*.pem` are exactly what an image
# accidentally ships when somebody adds `COPY . .` later.

**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.vs/
**/.vscode/
**/TestResults/

.git/
.github/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

**/*.user
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.pfx
**/secrets.json

docs/
benchmarks/
*.md
